        <obo:IAO_0000115>A construction that has been assembled by deliberate human effort.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>&quot;constructed&quot; should probably be made something like a quality and this class obsoleted or filled only by inference</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>constructed feature</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Some human constructions (such as the extra-planetary probes built for the Voyager missions) exist outside of Earth&apos;s (or any other astrononomical body&apos;s) technosphere, and are thus not astronomical body parts. Assertions regarding whether a construction is part of the technosphere of an astronomical body (e.g. Earth) should be made at the instance level, if needed / useful for the application case.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/envo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>human construction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
