                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A steep-sided valley on the sea floor of the continental slope. Many submarine canyons are found as extensions to large rivers; however there are many that have no such association. Canyons cutting the continental slopes have been found at depths greater than 2 km below sea level. Many submarine canyons continue as submarine channels across continental rise areas and may extend for hundreds of kilometers.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>canyon</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>canyons</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EcoLexicon:submarine_canyon</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FTT:421</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Geonames:U.CNSU</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Geonames:U.CNYU</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TGN:23415</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TGN:23416</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Submarine_canyon</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>SubmarineCanyon</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>undersea canyon</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>ENVO</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>undersea ravine</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ENVO:00000267</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/envo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>submarine canyon</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
