        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">The ridge frequently resembles the blade of a serrated knife. A French term referring to the bones in a fish backbone. Aretes are typically formed when two glaciers erode parallel U-shaped valleys. Aretes can also form when two glacial cirques erode towards one another, although frequently this results in a saddle-shaped pass, called a col.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://pubs.usgs.gov/of/2004/1216/a/a.html"/>
