        <obo:IAO_0000115>The lower terminus of a wadi where it widens into an adjoining floodplain, depression, or water body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FTT:157</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FTT:162</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Geonames:H.WADM</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>There is some ambiguity in this term, as wadis seasonally flood to become watercourses, while - at other times - are valleys. In this representation, the &quot;mouth&quot; of a wadi is only present when it is a watercourse.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/envo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label>wadi mouth</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
