            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The top-most layer in a thermally stratified lake, occurring above the deeper hypolimnion. It is warmer and typically has a higher pH and dissolved oxygen concentration than the hypolimnion.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EcoLexicon:epilimnion_</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
